From: GLM-EXL3-2x-GB10 testing line <tensorfold-zig-testing@local>
Subject: glm-cuda: the EXL3 prompt path in one call, written into the MoE slot rows; no target-MTP prompt absorption beside a drafter (Mia 1104 0007+0008, adapted to v1.2.3)

PROVENANCE: ported from MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-DGX-Sparks-1104,
patches/engine/0007 (a prompt pass's EXL3 experts in one call, written into
the MoE slot rows) + 0008 (no target MTP prompt pass beside a drafter)
(Apache-2.0, (c) MiaAI Lab) against TensorFold v1.2.3 (6ec5fa4cb), 2026-11-06,
by this line - a hand port (the fork's hunks drifted: our tree has no k6
kernels, the v1.2.x engine delegates the MTP absorption to
prompt_solo.mtpRows, and the two test files do not exist here - the test
hunks are dropped, the A/B's content gate verifies instead).

MECHANISM (0007): cuda_exl3.chunk_rows now follows cuda_state.prefill_rows
(2048 here; was 1024) - a prompt pass takes ONE call to the common EXL3
prompt kernels instead of two, so every expert's trellis decodes once a
pass instead of twice (~28 pairs an expert); a pair's sums do not depend
on which item of 64 holds it, so the bits are the same. The down kernel
gains yrow: with yrow set the caller points y at its own slot rows
([rows][yrow][dims], pair p = row*slots+slot at row*yrow+slot) and the
kernel writes there - dropping the cuMemcpy2D of [rows][8][4096] fp32
after every call and the prompt arena's y (bytesFor/scratchFor with
own_y false). The grouped (runSlots) path keeps its copy. yrow defaults 0:
the old ABI for every other caller.

MECHANISM (0008): with --drafter (DFlash2) every draft is the drafter
block's (cuda_lanes); the target MTP layer's caches are never read - yet
every prompt chunk absorbed every row into them, a whole DSA + MoE layer
a pass. prefillChunk and prompts.pass skip it when a drafter is loaded;
mtp_len stays 0, as snapshots and the next prompt expect.

MEASURED (Mia, RTX PRO 6000 sm_120): routed experts per 2048 rows 4.84 ->
3.50 ms (-28%) with skewed routing; one 2048-row call writing the slot
rows is byte-identical to two 1024-row calls and the copy; the MTP pass
took 28-41 ms of an 830-935 ms traced 2048-row pass (3.4-4.4%). In the
engine WITH 0009 (our adopted packed-s2), cold prefill 4K +12.6%, 16K
+15.6%, 64K +16.0%, T=0 replies unchanged.

PORT NOTES: exl3_experts.cu - our down kernel is self-contained (no
prompt_down template, no k6): the yrow ABI lands on its signature + the
write site. exl3_prompt.zig - Scratch.yrow (default 0), the
sizes/bytes/scratch For variants, run()'s guard + the down launch's
i(sc.yrow). cuda_exl3.zig - chunk_rows = prefill_rows, scratchFor sizes
bytesFor(false), run()'s fused path writes ey straight and skips the
copy. cuda_engine.zig/cuda_prompts.zig - the drafter guards. The test
hunks dropped (our tree lacks both files). STAGING: applies on v1.2.3 +
the 5-patch stack (verified byte-identical to the port commit on a fresh
checkout). OWNER: this line; STATUS: EXPERIMENTAL, judged by the exl3call
window (the content gate + the pp rows, the definitive protocol).

